The rule for conformance.kernel.grounding says the harness's grounding verdict is given "with no relaxation and the value-in-span check on" and returns "GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN". Changing the span from "foo" to "bar" while keeping value "foo" and document "foo bar" means the span still occurs but the value is not in the span, so the verdict must move from GROUNDED to VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN.